#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
  ~#goal: "Design a 26-step rigorous curriculum exploring raw TTY environments, logical programming (Prolog), functional paradigms (Haskell), graph queries (GQL), and terminal-based programming. Map these esoteric/foundational paradigms directly into Spw's linguistic and metacognitive architectures."
  ~#taste: "expressiveness, rigor, and metacognition through the synthesis of discrete classical paradigms into continuous semantic buffers."
}

^["stream"]{
  >>[2026-02-20 02:51] observe — The user is expanding the Mastery Curriculum from visual (HTML/CSS/SVG) to logical, functional, and terminal-based paradigms.
  >>[2026-02-20 02:51] decide — Synthesize a 13-step plan that bridges ancient terminal wisdom and robust mathematical typings with Spw's experimental syntax, creating a learning path for 'compiler as a collaborator'.
  >>[2026-02-20 05:55] revise — Expanded plan to 26 commits to ensure a fully nuanced deep dive into ANSI buffers, Unification, Monads, and Cypher before attempting the final CLI synthesis phase.
}

^["open"]{
}

